From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 19:36:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(input): apply server movement and camera permissions

Consume the core versioned permission channel for direct and ViaProxy connections. Filter gameplay key samples and recalculate the normalized movement vector before Java prediction. Camera locks discard mouse look while preserving menu controls and clearing smoothing history.

Send physical gameplay samples before local filtering only when the server advertises the raw-input channel. Suppress identical samples and resend the initial state on a new connection. This preserves Bedrock Script API input during movement locks without sending custom packets to ordinary Java servers or older core builds.

Clear permissions and sample history on remote disconnect and local world exit. Preserve held key state so controls resume when the server unlocks them. Manual mounting and broader vehicle comparisons remain incomplete.
